{"type": "pair", "at": "2026-11-27T13:24:58+00:00", "step": "advocate-20261127T132321Z", "issue": "whu-lean-orch-t1-q1-01e", "kind": "advocate", "seed": 272801755450641, "ruling_id": "6c10d329c6d5db7e", "prompt_sha256": "388a27cee450b3cd27c5dfc394cb63f39bfda40016ac6df96c67d1958d57ac11", "inputs_sha256": "b9b4b00804d217c5f11771aeb1d2fdc62227ed68d2c3a5bec4988d564070bea0", "first": {"ruling": "amend", "text": "We are not sure whether the tools change the number of women giving birth in a hospital (one study, 799 participants); the review rates this evidence as moderate certainty in its summary table but low certainty in its detailed table [2]."}, "second": {"ruling": "amend", "text": "The tools may make little or no difference to the number of women giving birth in a hospital (one study, 799 participants) [2]."}, "usable": true, "agree_decision": true, "agree": false, "usage": {"input": 3574, "output": 694, "usd": 0.028176, "seconds": 7.3}, "applied": false}
{"type": "pair", "at": "2026-11-27T13:25:01+00:00", "step": "advocate-20261127T132321Z", "issue": "whu-lean-orch-t1-q1-01e", "kind": "advocate", "seed": 272801755450641, "ruling_id": "47ba455a02c3da19", "prompt_sha256": "388a27cee450b3cd27c5dfc394cb63f39bfda40016ac6df96c67d1958d57ac11", "inputs_sha256": "3be8f94b8466fb228ba331fbf55c7ce9f96c013cb8945080f2e7f4643449015a", "first": {"ruling": "amend", "text": "Targeted client communication via mobile devices (TCCMD), compared with non-digital targeted client communication (e.g. pamphlets), may reduce any maternal health problem (RR 0.19, 95% CI 0.04 to 0.79) and any newborn health problem (RR 0.52, 95% CI 0.25 to 1.06) reported up to 10 days postpartum, based on low-certainty evidence, though the newborn interval includes both benefit and harm [3]."}, "second": {"ruling": "amend", "text": "Compared with non-digital targeted client communication (e.g. pamphlets), targeted client communication via mobile devices may reduce any maternal health problem (RR 0.19, 95% CI 0.04 to 0.79) and any newborn health problem (RR 0.52, 95% CI 0.25 to 1.06) reported up to 10 days postpartum, based on low-certainty evidence, though the newborn interval includes both benefit and harm [3]."}, "usable": true, "agree_decision": true, "agree": false, "usage": {"input": 2152, "output": 330, "usd": 0.015208, "seconds": 2.8}, "applied": false}
{"type": "pair", "at": "2026-11-27T13:25:07+00:00", "step": "advocate-20261127T132321Z", "issue": "whu-lean-orch-t1-q1-01e", "kind": "advocate", "seed": 272801755450641, "ruling_id": "4f61c7f89833e8ab", "prompt_sha256": "388a27cee450b3cd27c5dfc394cb63f39bfda40016ac6df96c67d1958d57ac11", "inputs_sha256": "56b1d9e778ab6b554241c4bceb5436de97cb2277f7aefc2a3e880700ea44d329", "first": {"ruling": "amend", "text": "For TCCMD versus digital non-targeted communication, effects on skilled attendance at birth are uncertain (very low-certainty evidence), and the intervention may make little or no difference to antenatal influenza vaccination attendance (RR 1.05, 95% CI 0.71 to 1.58; low-certainty evidence), though the CI includes both benefit and harm [3]."}, "second": {"ruling": "amend", "text": "For TCCMD versus digital non-targeted communication, effects on skilled attendance at birth are uncertain (very low-certainty evidence), and the intervention may make little or no difference to antenatal influenza vaccination attendance (RR 1.05, 95% CI 0.71 to 1.58; low-certainty evidence), though the CI includes both benefit and harm [3]."}, "usable": true, "agree_decision": true, "agree": true, "usage": {"input": 1980, "output": 645, "usd": 0.02082, "seconds": 6.0}, "applied": false}
{"type": "pair", "at": "2026-11-27T13:25:12+00:00", "step": "advocate-20261127T132321Z", "issue": "whu-lean-orch-t1-q1-01e", "kind": "advocate", "seed": 272801755450641, "ruling_id": "7279d53183592709", "prompt_sha256": "388a27cee450b3cd27c5dfc394cb63f39bfda40016ac6df96c67d1958d57ac11", "inputs_sha256": "f78bf88c87c2297eb2f6e6da4a8e8ec4935fcc02d2e873dca972b7952b2326a1", "first": {"ruling": "amend", "text": "Targeted client communication via mobile devices may modestly increase contraception use among adolescents compared with standard care (RR 1.19, 95% CI 1.05 to 1.35), based on low-certainty evidence [4]."}, "second": {"ruling": "amend", "text": "Targeted client communication via mobile devices may modestly increase contraception use among adolescents compared with standard care (RR 1.19, 95% CI 1.05 to 1.35), based on low-certainty evidence [4]."}, "usable": true, "agree_decision": true, "agree": true, "usage": {"input": 1122, "output": 373, "usd": 0.011948, "seconds": 4.3}, "applied": false}
